# Patterns that git-secrets should NOT flag.
# These are well-known public placeholders or synthetic test values.

# Supabase local-dev demo JWTs (iss=supabase-demo). These ship with the
# Supabase CLI and are public on Supabase's docs site; rotating them
# would mean breaking the local-dev DX for every contributor. The
# matching SECRETS_SCAN_HISTORY=true CI runs were flagging legacy CI
# workflow files (now removed: integration-tests.yml, test.yml) that
# committed these demo JWTs inline.
eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIi

# Synthetic supabase/config.toml jwt_secret (sub=homematch-v2-jwt-secret).
# Used only for local test-env JWT signing; payload is a label not a
# subject identifier.
eyJzdWIiOiJob21lbWF0Y2gtdjItand0LXNlY3JldCIs
